= entry .Inspectable2   the lower-priority home of `Inspectable.derived`, the total fallback
-   detail
+   detail

-       A trait which `Inspectable`'s companion extends, so that `derived` ranks below every
-       instance written in the companion. Not used directly; its `derived` is found through
-       the companion.
-   entry #derived   the instance for any type without one: borrowed, derived, or `toString`
-       Tries an `Encodable in Text` (marked `⸤…⸥`), a `Showable` (marked `⸢…⸣`), an `Optional`
-       type (`｢value｣` or `○`), a `Reflection` (structural, through `Inspectable.Derivation`),
-       and finally the value's `toString` (marked `“…”`). A type whose encoded form is escaped
-       or encoded must define its own instance, since the borrowed form would mislead.
+       Un trait que extiende el objeto compañero de `Inspectable`, para que `derived` quede
+       por debajo de toda instancia escrita en el objeto compañero. No se usa directamente; su
+       `derived` se encuentra a través del objeto compañero.
+   entry #derived   la instancia para cualquier tipo que no tenga una: prestada, derivada o `toString`
+       Prueba un `Encodable in Text` (marcado `⸤…⸥`), un `Showable` (marcado `⸢…⸣`), un tipo
+       `Optional` (`｢value｣` o `○`), una `Reflection` (estructural, mediante
+       `Inspectable.Derivation`) y, por último, el `toString` del valor (marcado `“…”`). Un
+       tipo cuya forma codificada está escapada o codificada debe definir su propia
+       instancia, ya que la forma prestada induciría a error.

=       or encoded must define its own instance, since the borrowed form would mislead.
